Group the `-v` symbol report by type, then file, then name

`axy -v` (with no source file) now lists the `.axysymbols` table grouped by type, then by the file that declared each symbol, then by name. Each file's entries sit under a `file.axy:` heading (e.g. `lib.axy:`) with the symbols indented beneath, instead of every line carrying a `file:` prefix — so symbols from different files are no longer interleaved.

The report shown after compiling a file now uses the same styling: the file's own variables, constants and labels are grouped under a `file.axy:` heading and sorted by name.

- README changelog updated.
